---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="ExCSV Tools & Libraries" description="CLI tools and libraries that read and write ExCSV.">
  <h1>Tools &amp; Libraries</h1>
  <p class="intro">
    Implementations of <a href="/spec/">ExCSV</a>. Both implement v0.6, including notes and links
    (<code>#note</code>, <code>link=</code>, <code>#link</code>), and both run the shared fixture corpus.
    Need a quick text ↔ JSON conversion? Use the browser
    <a href="/convert/">converter</a> — nothing leaves your machine.
    This list is curated — if you ship a library or CLI, open an issue on the
    <a href="https://github.com/boligolov/excsv" target="_blank" rel="noopener">spec repo</a>.
  </p>

  <section class="tool-list">
    <article class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-head">
        <div>
          <h2><a href="https://github.com/boligolov/excsv-golang" target="_blank" rel="noopener">excsv-golang</a></h2>
          <p class="tool-meta">Go · CLI + library · Reference implementation · CLI 0.0.6</p>
        </div>
        <span class="badge">v0.6</span>
      </div>

      <p>
        Reference command-line tool and Go library for ExCSV. Supports plain
        (<code>.excsv</code>, <code>.extsv</code>), row-ZIP
        (<code>.excsv.zip</code>, <code>.extsv.zip</code>), and
        <a href="/variants/#pack">pack</a> (<code>.excsv.pack.zip</code>) storage forms.
      </p>

      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li>Parse, validate, fix, and serialize ExCSV documents</li>
        <li>Header, metadata, rows, and conversion commands</li>
        <li>Computed columns (<code>formula=</code>): materialize / dematerialize</li>
        <li>Notes and links: <code>note add|list|remove</code>, <code>link set|list|remove|check</code> — unsafe schemes and unresolved anchors reported</li>
        <li><code>column rename</code> rewrites every reference — <code>formula=</code>, <code>#chart</code>, <code>#note</code>/<code>#link</code>, <code>link=</code> placeholders, pack <code>#fk</code></li>
        <li>Chart suggestions (<code>#chart</code>, <code>#chart-vega</code>): parse, validate, JSON mirror (library)</li>
        <li>ZIP wrap / unwrap / peek with <code>original-size</code> checks</li>
        <li>Pack <code>create</code> and multi-table <code>table list</code></li>
        <li>Fixture-driven tests against the shared <code>fixtures/</code> corpus</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="tool-install">
        <h3>Install</h3>
        <pre><code>go install github.com/boligolov/excsv-golang/cmd/excsv@latest</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div class="tool-example">
        <h3>Quick start</h3>
        <pre><code>excsv data.excsv validate
excsv data.excsv info
excsv data.excsv note add --row 2 --col amount --text "Refund pending"
excsv data.excsv link check
excsv data.excsv.zip zip unwrap -o data.excsv
excsv data.excsv pack create -o data.excsv.pack.zip</code></pre>
      </div>

      <p class="tool-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/boligolov/excsv-golang" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        ·
        <a href="https://github.com/boligolov/excsv-golang#usage" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Usage docs</a>
        ·
        <a href="https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/boligolov/excsv-golang/pkg/excsv" target="_blank" rel="noopener">pkg/excsv</a>
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-head">
        <div>
          <h2><a href="https://github.com/boligolov/excsv-python" target="_blank" rel="noopener">excsv-python</a></h2>
          <p class="tool-meta">Python 3.10+ · Library only · Alpha · 0.6.0</p>
        </div>
        <span class="badge">v0.6</span>
      </div>

      <p>
        Python reference implementation of ExCSV, ported from
        <a href="https://github.com/boligolov/excsv-golang" target="_blank" rel="noopener">excsv-golang</a>
        with matching module layout and error taxonomy. Supports plain
        (<code>.excsv</code>, <code>.ecsv</code>, <code>.extsv</code> sidecars), JSON
        (<code>.excsv.json</code>), row ZIP (<code>.excsv.zip</code>, <code>.ecsv.zip</code>), and
        pack (<code>.excsv.pack.zip</code>). The package version follows the spec: 0.6.0 implements v0.6.
        Pre-1.0 — pin a version and check release notes before upgrading.
      </p>

      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li>Parse, validate, fix, and serialize ExCSV documents</li>
        <li>CSV/TSV import, JSON and CSVW export</li>
        <li>Computed columns (<code>formula=</code>): materialize / dematerialize</li>
        <li>Chart suggestions (<code>#chart</code>, <code>#chart-vega</code>): checks, add / remove, JSON mirror</li>
        <li>Notes and links: resolve <code>row=</code>/<code>key=</code> anchors, build each cell's final URL with the scheme check, add notes and links</li>
        <li><code>rename_column</code> rewrites every by-name reference, sidecar-safe</li>
        <li>Row ZIP and pack containers, with optional AES-256 password support via <code>pyzipper</code></li>
        <li>Fixture-driven tests against the shared <code>fixtures/</code> corpus</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="tool-install">
        <h3>Install</h3>
        <pre><code>pip install "excsv @ git+https://github.com/boligolov/excsv-python@v0.6.0"

# or, for development:
git clone https://github.com/boligolov/excsv-python
cd excsv-python
pip install -e .            # core library, stdlib only
pip install -e ".[crypto]"  # + AES-256 zip password support</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div class="tool-example">
        <h3>Quick start</h3>
        <pre><code>import excsv

res = excsv.parse_file("data.excsv", excsv.strict_options())
doc = res.doc
print(doc.row_count(), doc.header.delim_name)

for n in doc.resolve_notes():            # #note lines, in file order
    print(n.target.value, n.row, n.col_name, n.text)
print(doc.resolve_links().cell_link(0, "order_id"))   # final URL, or None</code></pre>
      </div>

      <p class="tool-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/boligolov/excsv-python" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        ·
        <a href="https://github.com/boligolov/excsv-python#quick-start" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Usage docs</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="coming-soon">
    <h2>Planned</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>DDL generation from schema</strong> — auto-generate <code>CREATE TABLE</code> straight from <code>#column</code> definitions (today's <code>#$ddl:</code> lines are hand-authored). Streaming reads and file diffing are on the same roadmap — see the Go tool's <a href="https://github.com/boligolov/excsv-golang#status" target="_blank" rel="noopener">status table</a>.</li>
      <li><strong><code>excsv chart</code></strong> — render a file's <code>#chart</code> suggestions as text in the terminal. Both libraries already parse and validate charts; the renderer isn't written yet.</li>
      <li><strong><code>.xlsx</code> import / export</strong> — notes as Excel comments, links as real hyperlinks (<a href="https://github.com/boligolov/excsv/blob/master/docs/implementation/notes.md#excel-interop" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mapping</a>).</li>
      <li>Curious what's next for the spec itself? The <a href="https://github.com/boligolov/excsv/blob/master/plan/TODO.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">backlog</a> tracks it. No library at all? See the <a href="/cookbook/">CLI Cookbook</a> for <code>grep</code>/<code>awk</code> one-liners.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    max-width: 42rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .tool-list {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  .tool-card {
    background: var(--color-card-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.75rem;
    max-width: 48rem;
  }
  .tool-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .tool-head h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }
  .tool-head h2 a {
    color: var(--color-text);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .tool-head h2 a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .tool-meta {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .badge {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: #fff;
    padding: 0.25em 0.6em;
    border-radius: 6px;
    height: fit-content;
  }
  .tool-card > p {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
  .feature-list {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .tool-install h3,
  .tool-example h3 {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .tool-install,
  .tool-example {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
  pre {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .tool-links {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .coming-soon {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    max-width: 42rem;
  }
  .coming-soon h2 {
    border: none;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
  .coming-soon p {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
</style>
